# a comparison narrows its operand on the edges behind its Branch, and the narrower name stands for the operand in all that the block on the edge dominates.
# Each name is noted for the value and for all that had the value for their narrowest name, so twelve comparisons in one another leave a list of ninety names:
# long enough that a name is found by its value and then asked whether the list of the block holds it. Each arm still takes the name of its own edge, and none of an arm beside it.
# function steps(n) { if (n is an int32) { if (10 < n) { if (20 < n) { .. return n + 1; } return n - 1; } return n - 1; } return n; }
